<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lake Sevan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lake Sevan is the largest lake in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus">Caucasus</a>, lying at about 1,900 metres above sea level. Urartian kings conquered the tribes around it in the 8th century BCE and left inscriptions on its shores, and the monastery of Sevanavank was founded on its peninsula in 874. In the Soviet period water was drawn off for hydroelectric power and irrigation, lowering its level by about 20 metres.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lake-sevan.jpg" alt="Lake Sevan" width="320" height="290" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Copernicus Sentinel-2 L2A · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lake_Sevan_2022-08-14_Sentinel-2_L2A.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
